From: MidG971 <midgy971@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3568: Add domain-supply to NPU power domain

The RK3568 NPU power domain requires the VDD_NPU voltage regulator
to be enabled before the domain can be powered on. Without this,
the power domain driver fails to de-idle the NPU bus:

  rockchip-pm-domain: failed to get ack on domain 'npu', val=0x1ee

Add domain-supply property to the NPU power domain node referencing
the vdd_npu regulator from the RK809 PMIC.

This depends on the pm-domains driver regulator support patch.

Signed-off-by: MidG971 <midgy971@gmail.com>
Co-developed-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568.dtsi
index XXXXXX..YYYYYY 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568.dtsi
@@ -XXX,6 +XXX,7 @@
 		power-controller {
 			...
 			pd_npu: power-domain@RK3568_PD_NPU {
 				reg = <RK3568_PD_NPU>;
+				/* domain-supply provided by board DTS */
 				clocks = <&cru ACLK_NPU_PRE>,
 					 <&cru HCLK_NPU_PRE>,
 					 <&cru PCLK_NPU_PRE>;
